.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-receipt-status 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-receipt\-status \- Judge the named check\*(Aqs recorded receipt against HEAD and origin/main
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten receipt status\fR [\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-J\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIcheck\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Judge the named check\*(Aqs recorded receipt against HEAD and origin/main
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR [default: head]
Which git fact the receipt is judged against: the exact commit, or the branch
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
head: Keyed to the exact commit; an amend, a rebase, or a moved trunk expires it
.IP \(bu 2
branch: Keyed to the branch; every commit on it continues to serve the claim
.IP \(bu 2
named: Keyed to a value the CALL names, read through [`Rule::key_from`] (CLOUD\-987)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-J\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit byte\-stable JSON instead of pointer lines
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIcheck\fR>
The check whose receipt is judged
